      "content": "The lack of clearance in high-density racking creates a vertical \"chimney effect,\" which dramatically accelerates both heat and smoke movement upwards. This close vertical packing channels hot gases and superheated combustion products efficiently through the rack structure itself. Consequently, the fire transitions from a localized event to a large-scale, rapidly escalating incident because heat is efficiently fed upwards to ignite upper levels immediately.",
